<div class="qul-docs">
  <h2>About juz metadata</h2>
  <p>
    Juz data is exported in both <strong>JSON</strong> and <strong>SQLite</strong> formats.
  </p>

  <h3>Sample JSON</h3>
  <p>Here is an example of the JSON structure for the first juz:</p>
  <div class="docs-code">
    <div class="docs-code-header"><span>JSON</span></div>
    <pre><code>{
  "1": {
    "juz_number": 1,
    "verses_count": 148,
    "first_verse_key": "1:1",
    "last_verse_key": "2:141",
    "verse_mapping": {
      "1": "1-7",
      "2": "1-141"
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h3>Field descriptions</h3>
  <div class="tools-table-overflow">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Field</th>
          <th>Type</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>juz_number</code></td>
          <td>INTEGER</td>
          <td>The juz number (1 to 30).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>verses_count</code></td>
          <td>INTEGER</td>
          <td>Total number of verses in the juz.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>first_verse_key</code></td>
          <td>TEXT</td>
          <td>The key of the first verse in the juz (e.g. <code>1:1</code>).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>last_verse_key</code></td>
          <td>TEXT</td>
          <td>The key of the last verse in the juz (e.g. <code>2:141</code>).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>verse_mapping</code></td>
          <td>OBJECT</td>
          <td>A mapping of surah numbers to ayah ranges within this juz. For example, <code>"2": "1-141"</code> means Surah 2 contributes ayahs 1 to 141 to this juz.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
